# private-names-allow -- the default allow list for scripts/check_private_names.sh
#
# Ordinary English words that are not checked as bare repository names, because
# they appear in code, docs and commit messages all the time. One that is also
# a private repository's name is still looked for in the shape of a repository
# reference (`word.git`, "the word repo", `cd word`, a projects path, a
# host/owner/word URL). Only dictionary words belong here, never a project or
# repository name.
#
# Not read directly: check_private_names.sh copies this file to
# ${XDG_CONFIG_HOME:-~/.config}/script-helpers/private-names-allow when that file
# is missing or holds no terms. Add your own words there, one per line; this
# file is only the starting set. A word for one repository only goes in that
# clone's .git/private-names-allow.
#
